  "notes": "USAGE:\nA technical term used in both scientific and everyday contexts. Unlike the homophone {最近|さいきん} (recently), this word is written with different kanji and belongs to a completely different semantic field.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {細菌|さいきん}が{繁殖|はんしょく}する: bacteria multiply\n- {細菌|さいきん}に{感染|かんせん}する: to be infected with bacteria\n- {細菌|さいきん}{検査|けんさ}: bacterial testing\n- {細菌|さいきん}を{殺|ころ}す: to kill germs\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\nウイルス (virus) refers to a different type of pathogen. {細菌|さいきん} are living organisms that can be treated with antibiotics, whereas ウイルス cannot.",
